case that a lot of people are familiar with. But, but we've, we've implemented, I've certainly

00:38:08.336 --> 00:38:15.856
implemented my fair share of Bayesian models that, that run most of the time on diffuse priors.

00:38:16.497 --> 00:38:22.416
And the reason is because decisions in early phase get a lot easier to quantify.

00:38:23.057 --> 00:38:28.497
And it's, it's, you know, easier, easier to, because we talk about in statistics, right? We

00:38:28.497 --> 00:38:33.216
talk about statistical significance. Is this result just the, just the result of random chance

00:38:33.216 --> 00:38:38.497
versus practical significance? Do we have enough evidence of observing a large enough effect size?

00:38:39.057 --> 00:38:45.216
And because of the flexibility in Bayesian models, it's much easier to, and much more convenient to

00:38:45.297 --> 00:38:51.697
answer that second question. You can define, let's, for example, you can, you can more easily

00:38:51.697 --> 00:38:58.896
