00:40:08.737 --> 00:40:14.656
different view of probability. And, and it's, it's really useful just to, to use, probably to

00:40:14.656 --> 00:40:20.817
use it, to think of it as a quantification, a quantifying a way to quantify the degree of

00:40:20.817 --> 00:40:28.737
belief in something in general. So this is what's what my professor in grad school called the

00:40:28.737 --> 00:40:33.856
epistemic view of probability. It's a measure of how much we believe something, which is,

00:40:34.656 --> 00:40:41.377
which is more general and flexible and gets arguably more to the point than, than a frequentist

00:40:41.377 --> 00:40:48.497
definition of probability, which is just a long run ratio of, of repeated simulations of an outcome.

